\begin{defn}
An \emph{ordered ring} is a commutative ring which is also equipped
with a total order relation, $\leq$, such that:
\begin{align*}
	a \leq b &\lif a + c \leq b + c\\
	(a \leq b \land 0 \leq c) &\lif a \times c \leq b \times c
\end{align*}
\end{defn}

